      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T03:31:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function\u0027s call path is  `cros_system_hibernate` -\u003e `system_npcx_hibernate_by_disable_ram` -\u003e `system_npcx_hibernate_by_lfw_in_last_ram`.\nIn `cros_system_hibernate`, it already calls `interrupt_disable_all`.\nShould we move this code block to replace `interrupt_disable_all` in `cros_system_hibernate`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 253,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 261,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "a57a4983279e66331b23786546da7c93266de0e1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04e8beee_c530eb26",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/cros_system/cros_system_npcx.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 261,
      "author": {
        "id": 1390635
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-27T15:13:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please see https://chromium-review.git.corp.google.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/8623515 in this chain, it replaces `interrupt_disable_all` with explicit zephyr `irq_lock` calls.\n\nSee also https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/123232. Currently `interrupt_disable_all` is not compatible with `arch_cpu_irqs_are_enabled`.\n\nThis is part of a clean up to better align interrupt management with zephyr where possible to avoid similar bugs in the future.\n\n`system_npcx_hibernate_by_lfw_in_last_ram` is a special case where PRIMASK and BASEPRI need to be specific values. After crrev/c/8623515, `cros_system_hibernate` will call `irq_lock` (sets BASEPRI) which prevents this flow from being interrupted. Does PRIMASK need to be set sooner in this flow?",
      "parentUuid": "cdec6695_3bb437cc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 253,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 261,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "a57a4983279e66331b23786546da7c93266de0e1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e3131f69_24000b99",
        "filename": "zephyr/drivers/cros_system/cros_system_npcx.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 261,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T06:06:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I understand the background behind why these CL chains were introduced.\n\nSetting `PRIMASK` at the beginning of this flow ultimately guarantees that no ISR can interrupt it. This flow has only register accesses and not call kernel functions (no call to `arch_cpu_irqs_are_enabled`, unless `board_hibernate_late` touch it.)\n\nUsing `irq_lock()` should have the same effect, unless some private code sets an IRQ\u0027s priority to `0` without using the Zephyr API (e.g., by calling `NVIC_SetPriority()` directly). So it is not masked by `irq_lock`. \nI assume there are no such cases in the Chromium EC codebase.",
      "parentUuid": "04e8beee_c530eb26",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 253,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 261,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "a57a4983279e66331b23786546da7c93266de0e1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
